# One segment of data is acknowledged when the delayed-ACK timer fires
# (200 ms in this stack, inside RFC 1122's 500 ms limit), not at once.
0      listen 8080
+0     < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460>
+0     > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 <mss 1460>
+0.010 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535
+0     accept

+0     < . 1:1001(1000) ack 1 win 65535
+0.200 > . 1:1(0) ack 1001
+0     read 1000

# The stack's own data goes out at once, and the peer's ACK retires it.
+0.050 send 500
+0     > . 1:501(500) ack 1001
+0.020 < . 1001:1001(0) ack 501 win 65535
+0     state ESTABLISHED
